fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: bought_sergeant
name: Sergeant-at-Arms
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  level: 3
  role: standard
  armor: 1
  morale: 8
  weapon: Company blade, drawn second; the contract case, drawn first
  wants: The contract satisfied or voided. Either one ends the fight.
  special: HOLD THE TERMS — once per scene, the sergeant states the contract's boundary aloud,
    and every Blade in earshot at once behaves as though the boundary is where the sergeant
    just said it is.
  when_bloodied: Calls the Blades back to the boundary and starts offering terms out loud, still
    fighting.
  tells: It opens by reading the contract's terms aloud. This is not a bluff; it is how the
    company works.
  breaks: Surrenders the field the moment the contract is void (payment withdrawn, terms broken
    by the employer, or the named target gone), says so, and expects to be believed.
  twists:
  - The employer broke the terms an hour ago, and the sergeant does not know yet.
  - The sergeant has read the contract twice and privately thinks the party is right.
  - Two sergeants, two fours, and the fours have been told two different boundaries.
  - The named target is standing behind the sergeant, and is a friend of the party.
  - The contract case is gone from its belt, stolen, and the sergeant is improvising.
  - The party splits up, and the sergeant spends Hold the Terms to keep every Blade on one side
    of the line.
  nastier: Level 5, and Hold the Terms can be used again each time a Blade falls.
  description: The one reading the room instead of the target. Sergeants of the Bought carry
    the contract itself in a case chained at the hip and produce it more readily than steel
    — which lands strangely in Val'loh, where the written word belongs to the Church and a chained
    case of it is either blasphemy or a very expensive dispensation. Nobody at the gate is going
    to ask which tonight.
  notes: 'Level 3 standard, armor 1: no overrides.


    Reads first, fights second, and would genuinely rather not. Its first target is whoever
    is closest to breaking the contract''s boundary. It shifts for proof the employer has broken
    terms, and honours any deal that lets the company withdraw with its fee and its reputation.


    MODULE RESKIN (Oraga Night). Flavour fields only — name, description, organization and notes.
    Level, role, armor, morale and every card line are the Bestiary''s and must stay identical
    to enemies/bought_sergeant.fof; a test asserts it (INV-18). The Bestiary stays setting-agnostic
    (B9), which is why the Val''loh colour lives here instead.'
  organization: One per four Blades. Four of them are in Rekuzan.
  reskin_of: bought_sergeant
created_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
last_modified: '2026-09-25T00:00:00+00:00'
